{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובקרך וצאנך ירביון וכסף וזהב", :translit "u-v'karkha u-tzonkha yirbeiyun va-khesef va-zahav", :gloss "and your cattle and your flocks multiply, and silver and gold"} {:he "סמך כסף וזהב לצאן", :translit "samakh khesef va-zahav la-tzon", :gloss "juxtaposed silver and gold to flocks"} {:he "הרוצה שיעשיר יעסוק בבהמה דקה", :translit "ha-rotzeh she-ye'ashir ye'asok be-beheimah dakah", :gloss "whoever wishes to become wealthy should engage in small cattle"} {:he "ירבין", :translit "yirbeiyun", :gloss "they multiply"} {:he "חסר וי\"ו", :translit "chaser vav", :gloss "defective [missing] vav"} {:he "שאם מרעה בשדות אחרים", :translit "she-im mar'eh be-sadot acherim", :gloss "that if he grazes in others' fields"} {:he "נכסיו מתמוטטין", :translit "nekhasav mitmotetin", :gloss "his assets collapse"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition of silver and gold directly after flocks implies wealth through small cattle"} {:kind :other, :note "yirbeiyun written without vav signals that grazing in others' fields destroys wealth"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that one who seeks wealth should raise small cattle, as it is written: וצאן ובקר ירבה (Deuteronomy 7:13). The verse there links multiplication of flocks to blessing. Ba'al HaTurim sharpens this by noting that in our verse, silver and gold are juxtaposed directly to flocks, reinforcing the connection between small cattle and wealth.", :sources ["Chullin 84a" "Deuteronomy 7:13" "Deuteronomy 8:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition of silver and gold directly after flocks implies wealth through small cattle", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "yirbeiyun written without vav signals that grazing in others' fields destroys wealth", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:19.310945793Z", :model "glm-5.2"}